Find the Size of a MapTo find out how many elements a map has, use the.size()function:Examplemap<string, int> people = { {"John", 32}, {"Adele", 45}, {"Bo", 29} };cout 
  << people.size();  // Outputs 3Try it Yourself »Check if a Map is EmptyUse the.empty()function to find out if a 
map is empty or not.The.empty()function returns1(true) if the map is empty and0(false) 
otherwise:Examplemap<string, int> people;cout << people.empty(); 
  // Outputs 1 (The map is empty)Try it Yourself »Examplemap<string, int> people = { {"John", 32}, {"Adele", 45}, {"Bo", 29} };cout 
  << people.empty();  
  // Outputs 0 (not empty)Try it Yourself »Note:You can also check if a specific element exists, by using the.count(key)function.It returns1(true) if the element exists and0(false) 
otherwise:Examplemap<string, int> people = { {"John", 32}, {"Adele", 45}, {"Bo", 29} };cout 
